os ni errores en la contratación.\nQué se puede revisar: Comprobar si los contratos al límite abarcan necesidades distintas. Verificar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en áreas similares. Analizar si los contratos de diciembre se distribuyen por distintas áreas o servicios.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 32 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 3.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 10.7, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.6 to 21.2. December accounts for 34% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 27% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 4. Contract [1], for 14,754 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December suggests a pattern, but it does not prove improper actions. Similar trends could result from budget cycles or market conditions. The focus on small amounts does not indicate wrongdoing, as prices may vary within legal limits.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and amounts of contracts to see if they align with budget cycles. Review awardee A's contracts to determine if they repeat the same needs. Contract [1] shows a single instance of a near-limit contract, which may reflect standard procurement practices.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["VlGDVvfYzgZrhBlEHQFSKA%3D%3D","vvPoz06ZLMnIGlsa0Wad%2Bw%3D%3D","VwpM1jUf9wuIzo3LHNPGcQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}